"**Extends:** :class:`pybamm.expression_tree.unary_operators."
"BaseIndefiniteIntegral`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/unary_operators.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.unary_operators.DefiniteIntegralVector:1
msgid ""
"A node in the expression tree representing an integral of the basis used for "
"discretisation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/unary_operators.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.unary_operators.DefiniteIntegralVector:4
msgid ""
"I = \\int_{a}^{b}\\!\\psi(x)\\,dx,\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/unary_operators.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.unary_operators.DefiniteIntegralVector:7
msgid ""
"where :math:`a` and :math:`b` are the left-hand and right-hand boundaries of "
"the domain respectively and :math:`\\psi` is the basis function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/unary_operators.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.unary_operators.DefiniteIntegralVector:10
msgid ""
"The variable whose basis will be integrated over the entire domain (will "
"become self.children[0])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/unary_operators.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.unary_operators.DefiniteIntegralVector:13
msgid "Whether to return a row or column vector (default is row)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/unary_operators.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.unary_operators.BoundaryIntegral:1
msgid ""
"A node in the expression tree representing an integral operator over the "
"boundary of a domain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/unary_operators.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.unary_operators.BoundaryIntegral:4
msgid ""
"I = \\int_{\\partial a}\\!f(u)\\,du,\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/unary_operators.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.unary_operators.BoundaryIntegral:7
msgid ""
"where :math:`\\partial a` is the boundary of the domain, and :math:"
"`u\\in\\text{domain boundary}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/unary_operators.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.unary_operators.BoundaryIntegral:12
msgid ""
"The region of the boundary over which to integrate. If region is `entire` "
"(default) the integration is carried out over the entire boundary. If region "
"is `negative tab` or `positive tab` then the integration is only carried out "
"over the appropriate part of the boundary corresponding to the tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/unary_operators.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.unary_operators.DeltaFunction:1
msgid ""
"Delta function. Currently can only be implemented at the edge of a domain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/unary_operators.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.unary_operators.DeltaFunction:3
